# mutgap4_sys_iosfc_v1_width: A v1 descriptor's width is copied into the v2 form the map works on and reaches the IOSurface as kIOSurfaceWidth: v1 BGRA surfaces of height 8, an 8-wide one (bytesPerRow 32, 256 bytes) first, then 4096 wide in bytesPerRow 64, 17 wide in bytesPerRow 64, and 16 wide in bytesPerRow 64; each mapped then tested; each status and data page is locked. Measured: widths 4096 and 17 are refused (BadArgument), 8 and 16 map.
